From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Orchard migration <noreply@orchardlinux>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 09:33:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] power: supply: bq27xxx_hdq: Add the BQ27540 found in iPad
 5 and iPad 6

The iPad 5 (J71t) and iPad 6 (J71b) gauges are BQ27540 parts on HDQ,
according to their device trees from iBoot. They answer the documented
BQ27541 status, temperature, voltage, current and state-of-charge
registers, so match them with that register profile.

Cache-only mode is the BQ27545 profile's answer to slow Apple gauge
firmware; keep it there. The BQ27540 is read live so that charger
policy sees current values for battery current and temperature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../devicetree/bindings/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml    | 5 +++--
 drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq.c                  | 6 ++++--
 2 files changed, 7 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml
index 22d380efc..13433d7d5 100644
--- a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml
@@ -4,13 +4,13 @@
 $id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/power/supply/ti,bq27545-hdq.yaml#
 $schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
 
-title: Texas Instruments BQ27545 fuel gauge on an HDQ bus
+title: Texas Instruments BQ27540/BQ27545 fuel gauges on an HDQ bus
 
 maintainers:
   - Paul Praschl <praschlpaul@g-p.at>
 
 description: |
-  The BQ27545 is a single-cell fuel gauge which can communicate using the
+  The BQ27540 and BQ27545 are single-cell fuel gauges which can communicate using the
   Texas Instruments single-wire HDQ protocol. An HDQ device has no 1-Wire
   ROM address, so it is represented as the single child of an HDQ bus.
   D11 and D111 devices use Apple-specific gauge firmware whose
@@ -22,6 +22,7 @@ allOf:
 properties:
   compatible:
     oneOf:
+      - const: ti,bq27540-hdq
       - const: ti,bq27545-hdq
       - items:
           - enum:
diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq.c b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq.c
index 614f7dfd3..5ed8c7adc 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/bq27xxx_battery_hdq.c
@@ -105,8 +105,9 @@ static int bq27xxx_battery_hdq_add_slave(struct w1_slave *sl)
 	if (match) {
 		di->chip = (uintptr_t)match->data;
 		di->name = "battery";
-		di->cache_only = true;
-		di->cache_refresh_ms = 30000;
+		/* Only the BQ27545 profile needs cached telemetry. */
+		di->cache_only = di->chip == BQ27545;
+		di->cache_refresh_ms = di->cache_only ? 30000 : 0;
 		if (of_device_is_compatible(sl->dev.of_node,
 					    "apple,d11-bq27545") ||
 		    of_device_is_compatible(sl->dev.of_node,
@@ -149,6 +150,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id bq27xxx_battery_hdq_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,d11-bq27545", .data = (void *)BQ27545 },
 	{ .compatible = "apple,d111-bq27545", .data = (void *)BQ27545 },
 	{ .compatible = "ti,bq27545-hdq", .data = (void *)BQ27545 },
+	{ .compatible = "ti,bq27540-hdq", .data = (void *)BQ27541 },
 	{ }
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, bq27xxx_battery_hdq_of_match);
